# Chefaa Medications ≥1401: Evidence-Based Extraction Progress, Calibration, and Completion Plan

## Executive Summary: What We Have, What We Need, and Why It Matters

The dataset objective is a single, clinically credible JSON covering Chefaa products indexed 1401 and above, integrating commercial fields with core safety and dosing information. Evidence-backed progress includes seven detailed product packs spanning antibiotics, non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drugs (NSAIDs), a GLP-1 receptor agonist, an antihistamine, and a laxative. These products calibrate our schema, dosing and safety expectations, price normalization (EGP and SAR), and market context (Egypt and Saudi Arabia). Together, they demonstrate that Chefaa detail pages can consistently provide the fields necessary for a high-quality clinical dataset, albeit with expected variability in completeness by class and page.[^4][^5][^6][^7][^8][^9][^10][^11]

The immediate next step is a disciplined scale-up: batch URL discovery for high-yield classes (antibiotics; antihypertensives; anticoagulants; diabetes), standardized field mapping, targeted re-crawls where clinical detail is sparse (e.g., Augmentin), and rigorous QA on pricing anomalies and URL validity. This plan is designed to reach comprehensive coverage of the 1401+ slice while preserving clinical fidelity and operational efficiency.

