### Key Takeaways

- Schema calibrated. Field presence and variability are now well understood across major classes, enabling a robust extraction and normalization pipeline.
- Class-specific completeness varies. Antibiotics and NSAIDs offer rich dosing/safety content; antihistamines demonstrate interactions and storage; GLP-1 agonists require injection safety and monitoring; laxatives anchor adult dosing and onset.
- Risks mitigated via staged enrichment. Where pages defer to leaflets or present partial fields (e.g., Augmentin), we capture minimal viable records and schedule targeted re-crawls.

## Source Inventory, Page Architecture, and Sequence Anchor (≥1401)

Inventory and gaps. The corpus spans 130 page files with documented gaps and zero-result ranges. Subcategory summaries (nine groups; 168 products) provide secondary taxonomy for cross-validation and fallback enrichment. These guide therapeutic mapping and help stabilize class inference when detail pages are sparse.[^2]

Anchor for the 1401+ sequence. The tail slice is anchored to “ديكونادال” (Deconadal) 10 mg, 21 tablets on page 90. Enumeration proceeds via ascending page traversal, deduplication, canonicalization, and stable indexing, ensuring product 1401 aligns with the intended completion segment.[^16]

