### Validation Rules and Normalization

- Names: strip diacritics; collapse whitespace; transliterate to Latin; establish preferred English title case.
- Dosage and packaging: enforce patterns (“X mg,” “X mg/5 ml,” “X%”); unify pack sizes to “N units.”
- Categories: map to controlled vocabulary; subcategory hints resolve ambiguities.
- Prescription inference: by class norms and page-level signals; flag edge cases.

## Evidence Deep-Dive and Calibration Findings

Antibiotics: Augmentin 625 mg (10 tablets). Identification and pricing (117 EGP) are explicit; clinical detail is limited and deferred to the leaflet. This necessitates staged enrichment and validates the plan to capture minimal viable records for pages that reference leaflets.[^4]

Antibiotics: Floxamo 1 g (16 tablets). Fixed-dose amoxicillin 500 mg + flucloxacillin 500 mg; broad indications (respiratory, bone/joint, ENT, GI, gallbladder, typhoid, kidney, prostatitis, gonorrhea, skin/soft tissue, post-surgical wounds, intra-abdominal, dental abscess, middle ear, bronchitis, pneumonia, paratyphoid); adult dosing (1 g every 8 hours; oral); administration (swallow whole; ideally 1 hour before or 2 hours after food); contraindications (penicillin allergy); side effects (mild diarrhea, indigestion); pregnancy/lactation (consult physician); interactions (anticoagulants; other antibiotics); renal precautions; general storage; pricing (110 EGP pack; 55 EGP strip).[^5]

NSAIDs: Sapofen 400 mg (20 tablets). Ibuprofen 400 mg; COX-1/COX-2 mechanism; broad indications; dosing (1–2 tablets up to three times daily; max 6/day; not >10 days); administration (after food); contraindications (hypersensitivity; post–heart surgeries; peptic ulcers; severe hypertension; lupus; pregnancy); precautions (elderly; breastfeeding); extensive side effects (common and rare/serious); no drowsiness; manufacturer SPIMACO; price 10 SAR; alternatives listed.[^6]

NSAIDs: Nurofen children’s syrup (strawberry, 150 ml). Ibuprofen; analgesic/antipyretic/anti-inflammatory; indications (pain, inflammation, fever; colds/flu; toothache; headache; menstrual pain; joint/muscle inflammation); dosing (5–15 ml up to three times daily; tailored by weight/age; temporary use only); flavor (strawberry; orange available); pricing 17.15 SAR (alternative 15.3 SAR); market Saudi Arabia.[^8]

Diabetes: Victoza (liraglutide 6 mg/ml; 2 pens × 3 ml). GLP-1 agonist; indications (Type 2 diabetes in adults and children ≥10 years; adjunct to diet/exercise; cardiovascular risk reduction in adults with established CVD; weight loss adjunct); dosage (once daily; subcutaneous injection; abdomen/thigh/upper arm; rotate sites; do not mix with insulin; do not share pens); side effects (common: nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, appetite loss, constipation; serious: pancreatitis, hypoglycemia with insulin, kidney problems, gallbladder issues, severe allergic reactions); contraindications (Type 1 diabetes; hypersensitivity to liraglutide; concomitant liraglutide products; <10 years); comparative notes vs Saxenda, Trulicity, Ozempic; price 397 SAR.[^9]

Allergy: Telfast 180 mg (20 tablets). Fexofenadine hydrochloride 180 mg; indications (seasonal allergic rhinitis; urticaria; cold symptoms); dosing (adults and children ≥12 years: 180 mg once daily for seasonal allergic rhinitis; 60 mg twice daily as needed; urticaria 180 mg once daily); syrup dosing (infants ≥6 months; children 2–12 years); storage (below 25°C in a dry place); contraindications (hypersensitivity; avoid antacids with aluminum/magnesium); interactions (avoid grapefruit, orange, apple juices); side effects (headache, drowsiness, dizziness, nausea); safety (insufficient pregnancy data—consult physician; lactation—consult physician; non-cortisone); price 160 EGP; comparative positioning vs cetirizine, loratadine, dimetindene.[^10]

Laxative: Duphalac (lactulose 3.335 g/5 ml; 200 ml). Osmotic laxative; indications (constipation; treatment/prevention of hepatic encephalopathy; acute constipation); adult dosing (1–2 large spoons; preferably after breakfast; single dose; adjust per response; avoid doubling on missed dose); onset (~48 hours); side effects (nausea; mild vomiting resolving in days; severe diarrhea; electrolyte imbalance); pregnancy (consult a doctor); weight gain not expected); price 143 EGP (alternative detailed-section price ~87 EGP—flagged for QA reconciliation).[^11]

